add('coinchar','N Frequency','Characteristic','[Math.pow(Math.cos(p[1]/Math.sqrt(p[0])),p[0])]',lambda p:[math.cos(p[1]/math.sqrt(p[0]))**int(p[0])],'Sum N {N} independent symmetric ±1 variables and divide by sqrt(N). At Frequency {Frequency}, what real characteristic function results?','Independence multiplies characteristic functions. The standardized coin-sum expression approaches exp(-t²/2) at each fixed t.','p[0]<1||!Number.isInteger(p[0])',[1,-3,3])
add('roughness','Scale H','IncrementSD','[Math.pow(p[0],p[1])]',lambda p:[p[0]**p[1]],'A unit-scale toy fractional Brownian increment over distance Scale {Scale} has Hurst exponent H {H}. What increment SD results?','The power law specifies increment scaling. It describes a Gaussian process law rather than one rendered terrain.','p[0]<=0||p[1]<=0||p[1]>=1',[0,.01,1])
add('coast','Ruler Dimension Base','Length','[p[2]*Math.pow(p[0],1-p[1])]',lambda p:[p[2]*p[0]**(1-p[1])],'A stipulated fractal measurement rule gives Length=Base {Base}×Ruler {Ruler}^(1-Dimension {Dimension}). What measured length results?','A finer ruler raises measured length when dimension exceeds one. Real coastlines have finite scales where this idealization stops.','p[0]<=0||p[1]<1||p[1]>2||p[2]<0',[0,.01,1])
