add('heat','X Diffusion Time','Density Variance','[Math.exp(-p[0]*p[0]/(4*p[1]*p[2]))/Math.sqrt(4*Math.PI*p[1]*p[2]),2*p[1]*p[2]]',lambda p:[math.exp(-p[0]**2/(4*p[1]*p[2]))/math.sqrt(4*math.pi*p[1]*p[2]),2*p[1]*p[2]],'A toy diffusion starts at zero, diffusivity {Diffusion}, elapsed Time {Time}. What heat-kernel density occurs at X {X}?','The Gaussian kernel spreads with variance 2Dt. It is a continuum distribution, not a claim that one walker follows the mean.','p[1]<=0||p[2]<=0',[0,-5,5])
add('escape','Barrier Noise','TimeScale','[Math.exp(p[0]/p[1])]',lambda p:[math.exp(p[0]/p[1])],'A toy escape-time scale is exp(Barrier {Barrier}/Noise {Noise}), with prefactor one. What scale results?','The stipulated exponential captures strong barrier sensitivity. A physical escape-time approximation also needs a justified prefactor and regime.','p[0]<0||p[1]<=0||p[0]/p[1]>30')
add('decay','Initial HalfLife Time','Expected','[p[0]*Math.pow(2,-p[2]/p[1])]',lambda p:[p[0]*2**(-p[2]/p[1])],'Independent toy decays start with Initial {Initial} atoms and HalfLife {HalfLife}. What expected survivors remain at Time {Time}?','Independent random lifetimes produce a smooth expected population decay. Realized survivor counts still fluctuate.','p[0]<0||p[1]<=0||p[2]<0',[2,0,10])
